### Device locations on OpenStreetMap

The working OpenStreetMap example on [Maps, zones and location records](../home-assistant/maps-and-zones.html#labelled-locations-uncertainty-and-missing-data) uses the same base map colours. Its device markers are Accent green with a Primary green outline, and each has its own shape and letter. GOV.UK gives no road, building or river colours, so the example draws roads in White with Black tint 80% edges, buildings, railways and boundaries in Black tint 80%, and rivers and other narrow water in Teal tint 80% so that they stay visible. The Teal tint 80% coastal band also edges lakes and other inland water.

## In Home Assistant

The native Map card has its own map styles, and civica does not restyle it. Keep its provider attribution and its permissions. Use these colours for maps you design, such as a custom map or a picture of a map in a guide.

## Maintenance

GOV.UK values live in `docs/data/govuk-brand-colours.json`, under `pages.maps`, with the colours of the GOV.UK example under `pages.maps.example`. The working map takes its colours from `docs/javascript/map-examples.mjs`, and the browser tests check that they match the record. Run `npm run check:colours` after the docs build.
